  "issue_title": "Integrate validated repo sets into replay execution",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n#65 introduces a leakage-safe repo-set config format plus a strict loader/validator, giving us versioned, reviewable repo selection. It isn't yet wired into replay execution \u2014 this issue tracks consuming the validated repo set so benchmark runs draw their repos from the versioned config rather than ad-hoc selection.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `run_replay` / the multi-repo runner accepts a repo-set config path and loads it through `validate_repo_set`\n- [ ] Replay iterates the vetted repos from the config, respecting any leakage/eligibility constraints they encode\n- [ ] A run fails loudly on an invalid or placeholder repo set rather than silently proceeding\n- [ ] Tests cover config-driven selection end-to-end (offline)\n- [ ] `docs/architecture.md` documents the config-driven replay flow\n\n## Pointers\nRepo-set loader from #65, `benchmark/runner.py` (`run_replay`, multi-repo path), `docs/architecture.md`. Depends on #65 landing.\n",
